Starshine licensing scope
=========================

Joshua Tenner grants the MIT license below for original Starshine code and
original modifications that he owns. This grant covers only his own rights;
it does not relicense incorporated third-party code, translated/adapted
expression, third-party test fixtures, or compiler/library runtime portions.

The npm JavaScript facade, FFI-generated bindings and declarations, build tools,
and original consumer examples use this grant for their Starshine-owned parts.
Compiled Wasm also contains Apache-2.0 MoonBit Core and moonbitlang/x code, with
additional terms retained in NOTICE and licenses/moonbit-core-NOTICE.txt.
Apache-2.0 terms are supplied in licenses/Apache-2.0.txt; the full Binaryen
upstream license is preserved in licenses/Binaryen-LICENSE.txt.

The existing MoonBit module's Apache-2.0 declaration is retained. The owner
has authorized conservative upstream notice retention for potentially adapted
Binaryen pass expression while unknown provenance remains unknown. In particular, PickLoadSigns and
explicitly adapted Binaryen regression fixtures retain upstream terms and
attribution. Similar pass names, behavior or implementation language do not
establish independent authorship or grant permission to relicense upstream
expression. This distribution is not offered under an MIT-only bundle license
or a choice between MIT and Apache-2.0 for all included code.

See NOTICE for component scope and docs/wiki/tooling/license-provenance.md
in the source repository for evidence and unresolved pass classifications.

